            <p>There’s something delightfully giddy about sailing off toward Mexico. The shift happens gradually. The air is lighter, the sunlight gentler, and the horizon wide open. Going on a cruise to Mexico is not merely about reaching a beach destination. It is about the excitement that stirs as your ship sails through blue water toward colourful coastal villages and lively island ports. </p>

